{
  "description": "Reproduction for #17004 (from the design in #16948): a 45 mm cylinder with an arm joined to its side, a 7.5 mm chamfer round the cylinder's bottom, a 30 degree chamfer on the arm's end, two 13 mm rounds where the arm meets the chamfer cone, and a 2 mm round on the bottom arc and its neighbours. Two pieces of that 2 mm round are plane-to-cone rounds swept 0.45 degrees, stored as surfaces of revolution. Reading the body back into the kernel derived one of them about an axis 4e-11 mm off and refused it, so every later operation on Body1 failed with 'an exact net's NURBS form is not a surface of revolution's parametrisation'.",
